{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1082519-a-demon-went-down-to-georgia","id":1082519,"title":"A Demon went down to Georgia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-22T22:10:50-07:00","id":1082519,"title":"A Demon went down to Georgia","content":"So let's say a demon goes down to Georgia looking for a soul pack to seal. He meets a fiddle player named Johnny whose willing to make that deal. They arrange a contest in which Johnny will win a fiddle of gold if he plays his fiddle better than the demon. If he loses, the demon gets a new cover.<br /> <br /> Now! Brainstorm with me how we can transform this classic song into an actual pact. The rule as written don't really jump out at me with ways to make bets or games out of the traditional deal. But contests and competitions do pop up in deals with the devil, so I'd like to hear some thoughts on hacking the rules for this purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T07:36:21-07:00","id":1082604,"title":"","content":"Well, the terms of the pacts could invalidate Johnny's benefits if he loses the contest. The Demon might have a gambling streak or strong sense of pride for why they would ever do this thing.<br /> <br /> Pretty sure it is just basic conditions, not even needing rules representation.<br /> <br /> As an aside, this would be an awesome game/actual play title.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-23-2017, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T08:39:51-07:00","id":1082630,"title":"","content":"I would simply put it as some kind of mitigating factor (i think there was a forum thread about it), that the demon doesn't get the benefits if they lose the contest. Taking it as the same as a changeling's &quot;task&quot; condition we have:<br /> <br /> Johnny- benefits 1 (resources, golden fiddle) Mitigating factor -1 (must beat the devil in a opposed expression check to gain the benefits)<br /> The Devil- Soul 3, duration: Permanent (3), mitigating factor -1 (must beat Johnny in an opposed expression check to gain the benefits)<br /> <br /> That is a cost of 4 willpower points and 1 willpower dot. Conclusion? The Devil must <i>really</i> have been in a bind when he came upon Johnny","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T04:45:13-07:00","id":1082967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urbenmyth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1082519-a-demon-went-down-to-georgia?p=1082630#post1082630\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would simply put it as some kind of mitigating factor (i think there was a forum thread about it), that the demon doesn't get the benefits if they lose the contest. Taking it as the same as a changeling's &quot;task&quot; condition we have:<br /> <br /> Johnny- benefits 1 (resources, golden fiddle) Mitigating factor -1 (must beat the devil in a opposed expression check to gain the benefits)<br /> The Devil- Soul 3, duration: Permanent (3), mitigating factor -1 (must beat Johnny in an opposed expression check to gain the benefits)<br /> <br /> That is a cost of 4 willpower points and 1 willpower dot. Conclusion? The Devil must <i>really</i> have been in a bind when he came upon Johnny</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Probably burned his last Cover when he Went Loud. It's why he's appearing to Johnny in his full Demonic Form","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}